   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Reflexive pronouns in the accusative",
     "texto": [
      "When the reflexive verb doesn't take another direct object, the reflexive pronoun goes in the **accusative**: **ich** → **mich**; **du** → **dich**; **er/sie/es** → **sich**; **wir** → **uns**; **ihr** → **euch**; **sie/Sie** → **sich**.",
      "Key examples: **Ich bewerbe mich um die Stelle** (I'm applying for the job); **Wie fühlst du dich?** (How do you feel?); **Er ärgert sich über den Stau** (He gets annoyed about the traffic jam)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Reflexive pronouns",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Subject",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Reflexive (Accusative)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "ich",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "mich",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Ich bewerbe mich um eine Stelle.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
